> Only one request for @kleonc, do you have any id where the position is decided when you drag out from the sequence port?

After a little digging I think [here's the relevant part](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f00e3019984077a388ce7f117adb5483a8976016/modules/visual_script/visual_script_editor.cpp#L3121-L3163) (linked code includes this PR). As you can see it uses `port_action_pos` to determine the actual in-graph position. In the case you've mentioned `port_action_pos` [seems to be set here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f00e3019984077a388ce7f117adb5483a8976016/modules/visual_script/visual_script_editor.cpp#L2954-L2978). And indeed [this condition](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f00e3019984077a388ce7f117adb5483a8976016/modules/visual_script/visual_script_editor.cpp#L2965) doesn't check for output sequence port count so `port_action_pos` might not being set properly. [In `3.x` it's being set unconditionally](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c045219869dfccb507cdc60eeb93953c8730d8de/modules/visual_script/visual_script_editor.cpp#L3372). Will try to fix this in a moment.

@DavidCambre  And big thanks for the review/feedback!
